```csharp
public class BinarySearch {
    public static int FindIndex(int[] array, int value) {
        int low = 0;
        int high = array.Length - 1;

        while (low <= high) {
            int mid = (low + high) / 2;

            if (array[mid] == value) {
                return mid;
            } else if (array[mid] < value) {
                low = mid + 1;
            } else {
                high = mid - 1;
            }
        }

        throw new Exception("Value not found in the array.");
    }
}
```

This implementation has a time complexity of O(log n), where n is the number of elements in the input array.

