The algorithm initializes the distances for all nodes as infinity (or some large value), except for the starting node, which is set to 0. It then pushes the initial node into the heap.

Next, it repeatedly extracts the node with the smallest distance from the heap. For each edge connected to this node, it calculates the new distance and updates the `distances` map if necessary. If the new distance is shorter than the existing one, it adds the next node to the heap.

