The `rollback()` method iterates over all registered commands and rolls back each one if necessary.

Note that this is just a basic example to illustrate how a Saga pattern can be implemented in TypeScript. In practice, you may need to add more features such as retries, timeouts, or logging mechanisms depending on your specific use case.

